{"paper": "SSC-CPO-Tier1-29-Jun-2024-Shift3.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 50, "tagged_count": 50, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "11", "added": false}, {"text": "19", "added": false}, {"text": "57", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "An alloy contains the metals A, B and C in the ratio 2 : 3 : 1 and another contains the metals B, C and D in the ratio 5 : 4 : 3. If equal weights of both alloys are mixed together to form a third alloy, then how much part of the metal B is in new alloy?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mixture-Alligation", "sub": "mixture-price", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "-1", "added": false}, {"text": "0", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "triangle-and-quadrilaterals", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "increase-decrease", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "The following pie chart represents the data of movies released in a city throughout a year. The combined angle made by Jan-Mar and Jul-Sep is ____________ than the combined angle made by Apr-Jun and Oct-Dec.", "options": [{"text": "40° more", "added": false}, {"text": "80° more", "added": false}, {"text": "80° less", "added": false}, {"text": "40° less", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "pie-chart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "1∶3", "added": false}, {"text": "2∶3", "added": false}, {"text": "1∶2", "added": false}, {"text": "3∶4", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "Simplify the given expression.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "A dishonest dealer claims to sell his products at 24% loss on the cost price but uses 100 g weight instead of 200 g weight. His profit percentage is:", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "dishonest-dealer", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "34", "added": false}, {"text": "32", "added": false}, {"text": "28", "added": false}, {"text": "30", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "The side PR of a ΔPQR is extended to S such that QR = RS. If ∠PRQ = 86°, then find the value of ∠PSQ.", "options": [{"text": "43°", "added": false}, {"text": "86°", "added": false}, {"text": "54°", "added": false}, {"text": "94°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "Simplify", "options": [{"text": "60.456", "added": false}, {"text": "70.225", "added": false}, {"text": "57.426", "added": false}, {"text": "65.234", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "A shopkeeper sold 3 wristwatches for ₹2,800 each. If he has sold the watches with 40%, 25% and 12% profit, respectively, then find his overall profit percentage (correct to 2 decimal places).", "options": [{"text": "0.2455", "added": false}, {"text": "0.2475", "added": false}, {"text": "0.2419", "added": false}, {"text": "0.2463", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "profit-loss-percent", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "In a circle, the chords AB and CD intersect each other at point L (internally). If AL = 8 cm, LB = 6 cm and LD = 5 cm, then find the CL.", "options": [{"text": "10.6 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "8.6 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "7.6 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "9.6 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "circle-theorems", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "Two trains, P and Q, are running on parallel tracks in opposite directions with lengths of 110 m and 140 m, respectively. Train P is running at a speed of 70 km/h and took 5 seconds to cross train Q. The speed of train Q is:", "options": [{"text": "100 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "120 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "110 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "90 km/h", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trains", "sub": "two-trains", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "Simplify 45 ÷ 5 × 5 + 10 - 5.", "options": [{"text": "60", "added": false}, {"text": "30", "added": false}, {"text": "50", "added": false}, {"text": "40", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "34", "added": false}, {"text": "19", "added": false}, {"text": "17", "added": false}, {"text": "20", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "Simplify 250 + [100 - {50 - (30 + 15)}].", "options": [{"text": "280", "added": false}, {"text": "255", "added": false}, {"text": "360", "added": false}, {"text": "345", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "A man travels some distance from his house to the exhibition ground by an auto at a speed of 30 km/h and returns by a cab at a speed of 50 km/h. What is his average speed (in km/h)?", "options": [{"text": "37.5", "added": false}, {"text": "40", "added": false}, {"text": "28", "added": false}, {"text": "38", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "average-speed", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 21, "text": "The ratio of the speed of a boat to that of the current water is 35 : 8. The boat goes along with the current in 5 hours 10 minutes. What will be the time taken by the boat to come back?", "options": [{"text": "5 hours 15 minutes 58 seconds", "added": false}, {"text": "9 hours 30 minutes 49 seconds", "added": false}, {"text": "6 hours 45 minutes 10 seconds", "added": false}, {"text": "8 hours 13 minutes 48 seconds", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Boats-Streams", "sub": "upstream-downstream", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 22, "text": "Ramesh spent ₹30,000 on Diwali shopping and ₹45,000 on buying a TV set, and the remaining 40% of the total amount he had as cash with him. What was the total amount (in ₹)?", "options": [{"text": "1,35,000", "added": false}, {"text": "1,10,000", "added": false}, {"text": "1,25,000", "added": false}, {"text": "1,22,000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 23, "text": "If 12 people can print 540 identical books in 10 days, then how many more people will be required to print 720 such books in 8 days?", "options": [{"text": "8", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}, {"text": "12", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "group-work", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 24, "text": "A scalene triangle ABC has two sides whose measures are 3.8 cm and 6 cm, respectively. Which of the following CANNOT be the measure (in cm) of its third side?", "options": [{"text": "3.0", "added": false}, {"text": "2.4", "added": false}, {"text": "2.7", "added": false}, {"text": "2.2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "lines-and-angles", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 25, "text": "The area of a circle is 256π square cm. The length of its longest chord (in cm) is:", "options": [{"text": "32", "added": false}, {"text": "36", "added": false}, {"text": "34", "added": false}, {"text": "16", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "triangle-and-quadrilaterals", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 26, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "82.22%", "added": false}, {"text": "80.22%", "added": false}, {"text": "70.82%", "added": false}, {"text": "76.52%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "pie-chart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 27, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Mixture-Alligation", "sub": "milk-water-and-alloys", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 28, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "275", "added": false}, {"text": "180", "added": false}, {"text": "250", "added": false}, {"text": "220", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "bar-graph", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 29, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "complementary-angles", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 30, "text": "Sumit and Rajiv, working together, can do a job in 20 hours whereasSumit alone can do the same job in 25 hours. In how many hours can Rajiv alone do the job?", "options": [{"text": "90", "added": false}, {"text": "100", "added": false}, {"text": "70", "added": false}, {"text": "80", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 31, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "17.56", "added": false}, {"text": "20.82", "added": false}, {"text": "18.44", "added": false}, {"text": "19.78", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Elementary Statistics", "sub": "mean-median-mode", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 32, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "ratios-and-tables", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 33, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "1993", "added": false}, {"text": "1990", "added": false}, {"text": "1992", "added": false}, {"text": "1991", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 34, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "410", "added": false}, {"text": "405", "added": false}, {"text": "420", "added": false}, {"text": "415", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 35, "text": "Simplify the given expression.", "options": [{"text": "25", "added": false}, {"text": "15", "added": false}, {"text": "20", "added": false}, {"text": "35", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 36, "text": "If the length and breadth of a cuboid are increased by 6% and 8%, respectively, then the percentage increase in its volume (correct to two decimal places) is:", "options": [{"text": "11.48%", "added": false}, {"text": "13.96%", "added": false}, {"text": "12.96%", "added": false}, {"text": "14.48%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cube-cuboid", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 37, "text": "A shopkeeper offers a 10% discount on dairy products and still manages to make a 20% profit. What is the actual cost (in ₹) to the shopkeeper of a dairy product marked ₹420?", "options": [{"text": "325", "added": false}, {"text": "340", "added": false}, {"text": "350", "added": false}, {"text": "315", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "single-discount", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 38, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "expression-values", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 39, "text": "A seller marks an item for ₹500 and sells it at a discount of 25%. He also gives a gift worth ₹65. If he still makes 24% profit, then the cost price of the item (in ₹) is:", "options": [{"text": "320", "added": false}, {"text": "270", "added": false}, {"text": "250", "added": false}, {"text": "280", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "single-discount", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 40, "text": "The population of a town is 15000. If the population increases by 15% in the first year, by 25% in the second year and due to pollution it decreases by 6% in the third year, what will be its population after 3 years?(Round off number in answer)", "options": [{"text": "20269", "added": false}, {"text": "25269", "added": false}, {"text": "28269", "added": false}, {"text": "15269", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "population-and-depreciation", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 41, "text": "In an election, 95% of the total voters cast their votes. In this election, there were only two candidates A and B. The winner A, by obtaining 75% of the total votes, defeated his contestant B by 5500 votes. Find the total number of voters in the election.", "options": [{"text": "12,000", "added": false}, {"text": "11,000", "added": false}, {"text": "13,000", "added": false}, {"text": "10,000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 42, "text": "A student goes to his school by cycle. The distance from his house to school is 5 km and he covers this distance in 1 hour. While going he stops twice for 5 minutes each. Find his average speed (in km/h).", "options": [{"text": "5.5", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}, {"text": "6.5", "added": false}, {"text": "4.5", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "average-speed", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 43, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 44, "text": "A man borrowed ₹29,000 for 3 years and ₹45,000 for 5 years at the same rate of simple interest. If he paid a total interest of ₹62,400, then what was the rate of interest?", "options": [{"text": "18%", "added": false}, {"text": "20%", "added": false}, {"text": "27%", "added": false}, {"text": "25%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "rate-time-principal", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 45, "text": "If the radius of a sphere is increased by 20%, then find the percentage increase in its volume.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "sphere-hemisphere", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 46, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cone", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 47, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "11", "added": false}, {"text": "18", "added": false}, {"text": "17", "added": false}, {"text": "13", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 48, "text": "Find the value of [16 ÷ 2 - 7 × 15 ÷ 3 + {(1 + 4) × 5} + 4 × 3 - 10].", "options": [{"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "0", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "−2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 49, "text": "If a car runs at a speed of 60 km/h and takes 180 minutes to cover a certain distance, then what time will it take to cover the same distance at a speed of 40 km?", "options": [{"text": "4 hr 30 min", "added": false}, {"text": "3 hr", "added": false}, {"text": "3 hr 15 min", "added": false}, {"text": "3 hr 45 min", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "basic-tsd", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 50, "text": "Two rectangular sheets of paper, each 60 cm × 36 cm, are made into two right circular cylinders, one by rolling the paper along its length and the other along the breadth. The ratio of the volumes of the two cylinders, thus formed, is:", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cylinder", "key_answer": null}]}